load/t_thumb/sck391.jpg"}, {"id": 937334, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sck392.jpg"}, {"id": 937335, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sck393.jpg"}, {"id": 937336, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sck394.jpg"}, {"id": 937337, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sck395.jpg"}, {"id": 937338, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sck396.jpg"}, {"id": 937339, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sck397.jpg"}], "slug": "hook", "storyline": "Hook is an average game based on the movie of the same name, which is a modernized version of the classic tale. Peter Pan, who is now living a normal adult life, is compelled to relive his roguish past when his old nemesis Captain Hook kidnaps his children. Vibrant graphics, charming Tinkerbell as your sidekick, and decent puzzles can't hide the below-average writing, awkward interface, and the fact that the adventure is over all too soon.", "summary": "This version of \"Hook\" is a point and click adventure, and the pirate setting ensures that it recalls the Monkey Island games. The top 2/3 of the screen features a visual depiction of the area Peter is in, which a row of icons along the bottom can be selected to alter the function of a mouse click. These include looking at an object, picking it up, talking to people, using objects to solve problems (often in combination with others), and giving objects to others.", "themes": [{"id": 17, "name": "Fantasy"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/hook", "videos": [{"id": 190136, "name": "Trailer", "video_id": "SCpDbdXvhAc", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SCpDbdXvhAc", "title": "Hook - Complete Walkthrough (PC MS-DOS | Ocean Software | 1992)", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/SCpDbdXvhAc/maxresdefault.jpg"}]}